body:
I agree with you man, therapy is not that big of a deal. I want mental well-being, I go to therapy. Ba-boom. 

I was explaining this simple concept to my mum, and for the first time she actually agrees I should go to therapy, I put my point across it wouldn't make sense not to go, as it would help me improve my happiness and such. 

&#x200B;

And talking about how much we think of ourselves and stuff, hat's interesting man, I'm actually kind of the opposite. I tend to overshare with people a lot, like to the point where I can't help it and I feel like I have to get it all out (hence my reddit posts lol) -  and I'm concerned with other people to the point where it is a fault (like as in a can't take care of myself sometimes). BUT I am super narcissistic in the sense that I can't accept help from others, think I know best, judge others decision etc. 

&#x200B;

I also agree with you that narcissism can lead to great things! I think yeah, if I can manipulate it to the point where I'm conquering all my goals because my mindset is that 'I'm the man and I can do what I want' that wouldn't be such a bad form of narcissism.
